# --- OS / IDE Junk ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
.bin/
*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws
*~

# --- Go Binaries and Build Output ---
bin/
/goblinctl
/goblind
*.exe
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
*.test
_go-build/

# --- Protobuf Generated Files (Internal) ---
# Note: Keep generated code in repo if specifically required for build consistency,
# but usually internal/proto/*.pb.go should be ignored if generated on-the-fly.
# We follow a "check-in generated code" policy for GAPI/Goblin currently,
# so we only ignore intermediate buf artifacts.
buf.lock
buf.gen.yaml.lock
.bufbuild/

# --- Python Cache and build artifacts ---
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
venv/
dist/

# --- Nix Build Outputs ---
# No trailing slash: 'nix build' creates result as a SYMLINK to the store
# path, and a trailing slash matches only directories, so 'result/'
# ignored nothing nix actually produces. Same defect gapi carried.
result
result-*

# --- Temporary / Runtime State ---
tmp/
test/tmp/
*.log
*.pid
*.sock
gapi.db
gapi.sock

# --- Databases (common local state) ---
*.db
*.sqlite

# --- Generated Documentation ---
#
# GENERATED REFERENCE IS COMMITTED. docs/content/reference, docs/man and
# the pages under them are produced by `mage docs:generate` and checked
# in, so the reference reads on the forge without a build and the drift
# gate has committed bytes to compare against. Only the RENDERED SITE and
# the materialised magelib asset tree are ignored.
#
# The mkdocs-era patterns are gone with the targets that produced them:
# docs/_build/, docs/build/, docs/generated/ and site/ were mkdocs
# output. An ignore rule for a directory nothing writes tells a future
# reader the build still works that way.
docs/public/
docs/.magelib/
docs/resources/
.hugo_build.lock
# ANCHORED. Unanchored `man/` matches docs/man/ as well as the legacy
# root-level output, so every generated man page would have been
# silently excluded from the commit while `mage docs:check` passed
# locally and a fresh clone had nothing to compare. That is the same
# defect shape as an unanchored rsync exclude reading as a platform
# incompatibility: a pattern that matches more than it names, failing
# quietly. gapi hit this exact line; caught here by
# `git check-ignore -v` on a path the gate depends on.
/man/

# --- Mage Build Artifacts ---
mage_output/

# --- Air Live Reload ---
.air/

# --- Local Environment / Backups ---
config/*.local.*
config/*.backup.*
*.env.local
*.env.development.local
*.env.test.local
*.env.production.local
COMMIT_MESSAGE.md

# --- Coverage / Test Reports ---
cover.out
coverage.txt
coverage.xml
test-results.xml

# --- Scenario Build Contexts (Silo) ---
scenarios/goblin_cluster/build_context/

# --- TLS / Private Key Material ---
# goblin ships no key material and never should. This is PREVENTIVE, not
# a fix: test/cluster/gen_certs.go already writes its CA and per-node
# pairs to /tmp/goblin-test-certs, outside the repository, and no cert
# has ever been tracked here.
#
# The patterns exist because gapi demonstrated the failure mode - a test
# script writing into a tracked path put six 24-hour keys into history,
# every one swept in alongside unrelated work. Nothing structural stops
# a future script here from doing the same, so these make it require an
# explicit 'git add -f' to land.
*.key
*.pem
*.crt
*.cer
*.der
*.csr
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
id_rsa
id_ecdsa
id_ed25519
